<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="1"><Text>INT. FERRY TERMINAL - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Fluorescent lights buzz over an empty waiting room. DEE (30s), soaked from the rain, counts crumpled bills on a plastic seat.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A TICKET CLERK (60s) watches her over half-moon glasses.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>TICKET CLERK</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Last boat's at midnight. After that, nothing till Tuesday.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DEE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Then I'm on the last boat.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She slides the money across. It is not enough. The clerk pushes back two bills.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>TICKET CLERK</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quietly)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Pay me when you're back.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="2"><Text>EXT. FERRY DECK - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Wind and spray. Dee grips the rail as the island lights shrink behind her. Her phone buzzes. A text: "He knows you left."</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She drops the phone into the black water.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="3"><Text>INT. FERRY CABIN - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A cramped cabin. MARCUS (40s), in a good coat that doesn't belong here, sits across from Dee. He smiles like they're old friends.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MARCUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You threw away a perfectly good phone.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DEE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>How did you get on this boat?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MARCUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Same way you did. I paid.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He sets a photo on the table: a child on a swing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MARCUS (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>She asks about you.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dee doesn't touch the photo.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="4"><Text>EXT. MAINLAND DOCK - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The ferry bumps the pilings. Passengers shuffle off. Dee slips between two trucks and runs.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Marcus steps onto the dock behind her, in no hurry at all.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="5"><Text>INT. ALL-NIGHT DINER - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dee slides into a booth. ROSA (50s), a waitress with a pencil behind her ear, pours coffee without asking.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ROSA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You look like a girl who needs pie.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DEE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I need a car.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ROSA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Pie first.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="6"><Text>INT. DINER - BACK OFFICE - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Rosa hands Dee a set of keys from a hook. A faded photo on the wall shows a young Rosa with a child on a swing. The same swing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DEE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Where did you get this?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ROSA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Same place you did, honey. I left too.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="7"><Text>EXT. COASTAL HIGHWAY - DAWN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dee drives Rosa's old pickup into the sunrise. In the rearview mirror, headlights. Far back, but there.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She presses the gas. The headlights keep pace.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="8"><Text>EXT. CLIFFSIDE PULLOUT - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dee pulls over. The headlights pull in behind her. Marcus gets out, hands up, the photo in one of them.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MARCUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I'm not here to take you back.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DEE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Then why are you here?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MARCUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Because she's sick. And you're the only match.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Dee looks at the photo, then at the sea. Long silence.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>DEE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Get in.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>FADE OUT.</Text></Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>